          "0": {
            "id": "14010687",
            "headline": "Tempsens Instruments raises over Rs 194 cr via anchor book; Rs 650 cr IPO opens August 20",
            "heading": "Tempsens Instruments raises over Rs 194 cr via anchor book; Rs 650 cr IPO opens August 20",
            "intro": "Tempsens Instruments IPO | The company is hitting Dalal Street with a target to mobilise Rs 650 crore through its initial public offering.",
            "body": "Leading contact and non-contact temperature sensor maker Tempsens Instruments (India) has raised Rs 194.5 crore through its anchor book on August 19, a day before the IPO opens for subscription.\r\n\r\nThe company is hitting Dalal Street with a target to mobilise Rs 650 crore through its initial public offering (IPO), which will open on August 20 and close on August 24.\r\n\r\nThe price band for the IPO, which comprises a fresh issue of shares worth Rs 95 crore and an offer-for-sale (OFS) of 1.85 crore shares amounting to Rs 555 crore, has been fixed at Rs 285-300 per share.\r\n\r\nTempsens Instruments on Wednesday issued 64.84 lakh equity shares to 29 anchor investors, including Singaporean Temasek Holdings-owned Aranda Investments, Goldman Sachs, and Prashant Khemka's Ashoka WhiteOak ICAV - Ashoka WhiteOak Emerging Markets Equity Fund.\r\n\r\nOf the total anchor book, 37.21 lakh shares were allocated to eight domestic mutual funds, including HDFC AMC, Nippon Life India, Kotak Mahindra AMC, Aditya Birla Sun Life AMC, Edelweiss and Tata Mutual Fund, which applied through a total of 14 schemes, the company said in its filing.\r\n\r\nFurther, 4.67 lakh shares were allocated to Axis Max Life Insurance and Kotak Mahindra Life Insurance.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nWith 15 manufacturing units globally, Tempsens Instruments claims to be the largest manufacturer of contact and non-contact temperature sensors in India, with a market share of 10.5% in the temperature sensor segment and 21.3% in the non-contact temperature sensor market.\r\n\r\nDomestic business contributed 71.5% to the topline in FY26, while the remaining 28.5% came from exports. The company reported a profit of Rs 67.3 crore for the fiscal year ended March 2026, up 11.2% from Rs 60.6 crore in the previous year. Revenue increased 17.5% to Rs 444.9 crore from Rs 378.5 crore during the same period.\r\n\r\nRajasthan-based thermal engineering and specialised cable manufacturer Tempsens Instruments will spend Rs 18.1 crore of the net proceeds from the fresh issue on capital expenditure towards electrical heating solutions and specialised cable solutions.\r\n\r\nFurther, Rs 55 crore will be utilised for repaying debt, while the remaining funds will be used for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nICICI Securities and JM Financial are acting as the merchant bankers for the Tempsens Instruments IPO.",
