          "1": {
            "id": "14010503",
            "headline": "Annu Projects IPO to open on August 25, listing likely on September 2",
            "heading": "Annu Projects IPO to open on August 25, listing likely on September 2",
            "intro": "Annu Projects IPO | The offer comprises an entirely fresh issue of 1.76 crore equity shares.",
            "body": "Annu Projects, a New Delhi-based EPC company with a special focus on underground and overhead utilities infrastructure, has finalised August 25 as the opening date for its IPO for public subscription.\r\n\r\nThe IPO comprises an entirely fresh issue of 1.76 crore equity shares, with no offer-for-sale component, according to the red herring prospectus filed with the Registrar of Companies on August 18.\r\n\r\nThe issue size has been reduced from the 2.2 crore fresh equity shares planned in the draft document filed with SEBI in June 2025. Subsequently, the capital markets regulator cleared the IPO papers in November 2025.\r\n\r\nThe price band for the offer will be announced separately in the next couple of sessions.\r\n\r\nThe issue will remain open until August 28. The IPO share allotment is expected to be finalised by August 31, while Annu Projects shares are likely to be listed on the bourses on September 2.\r\n\r\nAnnu Projects claims to be one of the diversified companies in the EPC sector, undertaking fibre optics, sewerage and gas pipeline projects. The company has completed 362 projects over the last 21 years and has 23 ongoing projects as of June 2026. Of these, four projects each are in the telecom and gas pipeline infrastructure segments, while 14 are in sewerage infrastructure.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nOf the total basic contract value of Rs 1,681.4 crore, the company has completed work amounting to Rs 676.4 crore, while its outstanding order book stood at Rs 1,005 crore as of June 2026.\r\n\r\nThe infrastructure services provider will spend Rs 15.4 crore of the net IPO proceeds on the purchase of machinery and equipment. A further Rs 115 crore will be utilised for its working capital requirements, with the remaining funds earmarked for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nOn the financial front, the company reported a standalone profit of Rs 33 crore and revenue of Rs 241.2 crore for the fiscal year ended March 2026.\r\n\r\nMefcom Capital Markets has been appointed as the merchant banker to manage the Annu Projects IPO.\r\n\r\nMeanwhile, with the Annu Projects IPO, the mainboard segment will see four maiden public issues next week, including Symbiotec Pharmalab, Hy-Tech Engineers and Skyways Air Services, all three of which will open on August 24.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/annu-projects-ipo-to-open-on-august-25-listing-likely-on-september-2-14010503.html",
