          "2": {
            "id": "14010473",
            "headline": "Upcoming IPOs: Augmont Enterprises, Symbiotec, Skyways Air GMPs rise up to 29% ahead of issue opening - Check details",
            "heading": "Upcoming IPOs: Augmont Enterprises, Symbiotec, Skyways Air GMPs rise up to 29% ahead of issue opening - Check details",
            "intro": "Shares of Skyways Air Services are commanding a GMP of about 29 percent.",
            "body": "The grey market premium (GMP) for shares of Augmont Enterprises and Skyways Air Services has risen ahead of their initial public offerings (IPOs), while Symbiotec Pharmalab shares are commanding a flat premium, according to platforms tracking grey market activities.\r\n\r\nShares of Augmont Enterprises are commanding a GMP of up to 24 per cent. Investorgain quoted a GMP of Rs 190 for the shares, indicating a listing gain of 24.11 per cent. IPO Watch also quoted a GMP of 24 per cent.\r\n\r\nAugmont Enterprises, a Mumbai-based gold and silver platform serving businesses and consumers, will open its Rs 825-crore IPO for public subscription on August 21.\r\n\r\nThe price band for the issue has been fixed at Rs 750-788 per share, valuing the company at Rs 7,200 crore.\r\n\r\nMeanwhile, shares of Symbiotec Pharmalab are commanding a flat GMP, according to the platforms tracking grey market activities.\r\n\r\nThe Madhya Pradesh-based contract development and manufacturing organisation, backed by Rosewood Corporation and Motilal Oswal, has decided to open its maiden public issue amounting to Rs 1,757 crore on August 24.\r\n\r\nThis would be the second mainboard IPO to open next week, alongside the public issue of Skyways Air Services.\r\n\r\nShares of Skyways Air Services are commanding a GMP of about 29 per cent, according to grey market tracking platforms.\r\n\r\nThe Delhi-based air freight forwarding and logistics company will open its IPO for public subscription on August 24. The issue comprises a fresh issue of shares as well as an offer-for-sale (OFS).\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: The views and investment tips expressed by investment experts on Moneycontrol.com are their own and not those of the website or its management. Moneycontrol.com advises users to check with certified experts before taking any investment decisions.",
